[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'There is a huge problem with how AI agents get data from the web because right now a scraper will get all the rendered HTML from a page and a parser will parse it to markdown for agents to understand. But in most cases a page is'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'rendering data it fetched from the backend. So a scraper is getting all these extra HTML characters and a parser has to go through it to extract the exact same information that the page got'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in the first place. Wouldn\'t it be easier just get that information directly? This is why we built Alexandria, a knowledge library with over 113 million indexed sources from over 100'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'providers including Skyscanner, ESPN, Hugging Face, Wayback Machine, and much more. Giving your agents direct access to all this data in one place and you can use Alexandria right now. So I can'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'open up an agent like Claude code and I could prompt find series A fintech companies in New York with this amount of employees and get me the head of marketing giving me their work emails.'

